WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.170
Meet Trevor Hawthorn, now known as D-4651.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.660
On the outside, he was an armed robber who
murdered two people during a convenience store

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.190
shoot-out in Texas.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:16.440
But now, since being condemned to death, he’s
been picked up for D-Class testing by the

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.390
SCP Foundation.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:23.850
Now also meet Junior Researcher Dr. Julia
Reed - an aspiring Foundation scientist with

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.150
an undiagnosed heart condition.

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:31.330
The kind of heart condition that doesn’t
mix well with a high-pressure job at The SCP

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:32.330
Foundation.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:38.059
These two woke up on the morning of December
6th, 2011, completely unaware of the fact

00:00:38.059 --> 00:00:42.210
they were only hours away from causing one
of the most devastating containment breaches

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.629
Site 19 had seen in years.

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:51.940
Many people died that day, but thankfully
for everyone else, SCP-131 were there to save

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:52.940
the day.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:57.249
When you think of a hero, you probably don’t
picture a pair of little cyborgs with one

00:00:57.249 --> 00:01:02.039
eye and the intelligence of a household cat,
but this is the tale of how two of the most

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:08.119
unassuming anomalies at Site 19 managed to
save thousands of people from two of the Site’s

00:01:08.119 --> 00:01:10.500
most dangerous inmates.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.579
Open your eyes, and keep them open.

00:01:12.579 --> 00:01:16.000
If you so much as blink, it’s all over for
you.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.619
How long can you hold it?

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:18.759
Difficult, right?

00:01:18.759 --> 00:01:23.659
Now imagine you’re having a staring contest
with an entity that can kill you if you dare

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:26.560
to blink for even a fraction of a second.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:32.850
Or, even worse, a creature that could potentially
kill hundreds or even thousands of people

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:36.479
if your attention drifts from it for any amount
of time.

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:39.340
Try keeping your eyes open with that kind
of crushing pressure.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:43.970
We’re talking about two of the most deadly
Euclid and Keter Class anomalies out there

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:51.140
- SCP-173, the Killer Sculpture, a violent
Euclid-class entity that is incapable of moving

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:52.340
while being looked at.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:57.090
If ever it’s unobserved, it’ll snap the
neck of anyone nearby.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:03.119
SCP-689, known as Haunter in the Dark, is
an equally dangerous and even more attention

00:02:03.119 --> 00:02:04.979
demanding statue.

00:02:04.979 --> 00:02:11.849
These two entities are beyond dangerous - even
SCP-682 is terrified of the Killer Sculpture,

00:02:11.849 --> 00:02:16.950
and researchers have been considering the
use of 689 to potentially eliminate the hard-to-destroy

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.560
reptile for quite some time.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.870
Their greatest concern though, is whether
the 30-centimeter-tall statue would cause

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:28.560
too much collateral damage to Foundation personnel
in the process.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:34.780
Trevor Hawthorn was part of the three-man
D-class detail meant to clean out SCP-173’s

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.840
containment chamber at regular intervals.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.010
While on cleaning duty, two D-Classes can
keep staring at the Sculpture while the other

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.440
tidies up the cell, alternating turns to blink.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:50.129
But that morning, Trevor had woken up in his
containment cell with a killer migraine, and

00:02:50.129 --> 00:02:54.659
soon, that migraine would be killing far more
than just him.

00:02:54.659 --> 00:02:58.799
The containment procedures in 689’s cell
were also a three person job.

00:02:58.799 --> 00:03:05.180
689 is a small, green soapstone statue of
a skeletal being sitting on a throne, believed

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:10.840
to be some form of underworld death deity
discovered by German archaeologists in India.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:15.420
This is a work of religious art that demands
your attention, or you and anyone else who’s

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:20.380
ever seen this Keter-class nightmare will
suffer a horrifying fate.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:24.500
Anyone who’s ever seen the statue is “infected”
by its anomalous effects.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:28.829
It must be observed constantly, or someone
who’s seen it in the past will suddenly

00:03:28.829 --> 00:03:34.880
drop dead of a severe health issue like a
stroke or multiple rupturing organs.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:39.310
Like the God of Death the statue represents,
it appears on top of the dead body of whoever

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:40.709
it just killed.

00:03:40.709 --> 00:03:45.660
If not continually paid attention to, it’ll
keep hopping from person to person until it’s

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.000
killed everyone who’s ever looked at it.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.540
Its teleporting abilities, and the fact that
it poses a threat to so many, make this a

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.430
truly formidable foe.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:59.660
It’s kept in a constantly-lit cell, and
is observed by two members of D-Class personnel

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.569
at all times.

00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:07.180
But a crucial third party in the containment
of SCP - 689 is a member of personnel at Level

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.349
2 or above.

00:04:08.349 --> 00:04:14.200
They remain in a control room, wearing a special
visor to prevent them from ever seeing 689

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.920
and becoming infected themselves.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:21.139
If the containment fails, it’s their job
to throw the kill switch on the D-Class observers

00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:24.039
to prevent them from becoming vectors for
infection.

00:04:24.039 --> 00:04:27.450
Today, this job fell on Dr. Julia Reed.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:32.500
She was linked to the two observers via an
audio feed, allowing her to remain in constant

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:37.500
contact with them, and she had her finger
on the activation key for a pair of explosive

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:40.750
collars that were around the D-Class’ necks.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.830
Little did they know, Dr. Reed’s heart was
its own time bomb.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:50.600
Now you know what we’re up against: A snap-happy
Sculpture, and a teleporting death statue

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:54.720
with a hit list containing everyone who’s
ever glanced at it.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:57.650
What can SCP - 131 bring to the table?

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:03.970
The two small, cycloptic anomalies have only
one remarkable ability: They never blink.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.610
That and a soft spot for humans.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:11.610
These Safe-Class SCPs pose no threat to their
handlers, and can even form attachments to

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:15.160
researchers and other staff who show affection
towards them.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:19.720
Of course, forming these bonds is discouraged
by Site 19’s Director because it can be

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:23.150
distracting, but that doesn’t mean it doesn’t
happen.

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:30.600
The two Eye Pods, known as SCP-131-A and SCP-131-B,
are identical in appearance except for their

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.600
colors.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:35.120
A is burnt orange, and B is mustard yellow.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:39.690
The two of them appear to communicate with
one another via high-pitched squeaking noises,

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:44.170
and also seem to have an innate ability to
detect danger occurring in the vicinity, as

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:48.140
well as danger occurring near individuals
they’ve bonded with.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:52.620
Because of their inability to cause harm and
their generally affectionate demeanor, the

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:57.639
Eye Pods are allowed to roam around Site 19,
provided they keep out of the way of researchers

00:05:57.639 --> 00:05:59.770
and stay out of restricted areas.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:04.810
They seem to pretty much stick to the rules,
though check-ins on A and B are required every

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:06.690
hour, just to be safe.

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:11.130
As the Eye Pods were moving freely around
the facility, Trevor and another D-Class maintained

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:15.669
a visual on the Sculpture in its containment
chamber while a third man swept up the mixture

00:06:15.669 --> 00:06:19.430
of blood and excrement staining the concrete
floors.

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:23.420
Things were going fine, until Trevor’s migraine
got the better of him.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:29.090
A sudden flash of intense pain shot through
his head, and in a moment of weakness he made

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:30.840
a terrible mistake.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:35.870
With an audible groan of pain, Trevor closed
his eyes and forced his fingers to his temples.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:39.880
The groan had taken his fellow observer off
guard, and the man’s eyes flitted over to

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.910
him for a fraction of a second.

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:45.190
But a fraction of a second is all the Sculpture
needs.

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:50.250
In an instant, Trevor and his fellow watcher
had their necks snapped, and the third D-Class

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:54.000
was murdered before he even had the chance
to turn around.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.690
Containment protocol dictates that the door
is to be sealed behind the cleaning crew while

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:02.870
they’re working with 173, but this time,
perhaps due to complacency, the guards had

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:05.160
neglected to reinforce the door.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:09.420
They got their heads twisted a hundred and
eighty degrees for their trouble.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.660
SCP-173 was loose.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:16.009
Mobile Task Forces were dispatched to aid
in the re-containment effort as 173 began

00:07:16.009 --> 00:07:21.240
wreaking havoc around the facility, but things
were about to get even worse.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:26.470
It seemed like business as usual over at the
containment cell of SCP-689.

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:31.210
Two D-Classes observed while Dr. Reed dictated
to them over an earpiece from her control

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:32.210
center.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:37.490
However, what Dr. Reed thought were just minor
chest pains was actually the onset of heart

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:38.490
failure.

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:42.890
When the two D-Classes heard their supervisor
experiencing a fatal heart attack on the other

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:45.720
end of the line, they began to panic.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:50.940
This meant their attention wasn’t entirely
on SCP-689, and they were further distracted

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:57.729
by the chaos SCP - 173 was causing elsewhere
in the facility: murdering researchers, guards,

00:07:57.729 --> 00:08:01.300
and maintenance workers alike which led to
power outages.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.819
The lights in 689’s containment cell shut
down.

00:08:04.819 --> 00:08:10.710
Guards were dispatched to execute the observers,
as is protocol for 689 containment breaches,

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:15.970
but the fact that resources were already stretched
thin by the 173 breach caused a fatal error

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:19.030
in judgment from a guard posted nearby.

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:23.509
In a panic, he opened the door to find one
D-Class dead with the statue perched on his

00:08:23.509 --> 00:08:27.699
body and the other one running straight for
him in blind fear.

00:08:27.699 --> 00:08:30.590
The two collided and tumbled out into the
hall.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:36.610
Both were now infected by 689’s anomalous
attention, and both were now doomed.

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:41.570
Moments later, the two of them were dead,
the statue perched on their bodies, accidentally

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:47.130
catching the eye of several researchers and
guards running to deal with the 173 situation.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:52.860
For these two deadly anomalies, it was becoming
an all-you-can-kill buffet.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:58.050
The staff of Site 19 were now dealing with
one anomaly that needed to be looked at constantly,

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:02.550
and another that if you even glance at it,
you are effectively infected with a fatal

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:03.780
disease.

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:08.740
The Eye Pods, sensing an imminent danger nearby,
immediately sprung into action.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:13.920
It would be up to these cute, harmless anomalies
to save the terrified staff during this chaotic

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.820
double-containment breach.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:21.140
In a nearby hallway, a fleeing Foundation
researcher heard the crunches of her colleagues’

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:23.090
necks breaking behind her.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:25.290
173 was getting closer.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:27.380
This thing couldn’t be outrun.

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:32.950
She turned, and saw the statue standing there,
just ten feet away from her, a dead researcher

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:35.210
laying on the ground in front of it.

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:38.450
She was locked in a deadly staring contest
with The Sculpture.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:42.880
How long she could survive was now dependent
on how long she could keep her eyes open,

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:45.210
and it was getting harder by the second.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.030
She could feel her eyes drying.

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:49.480
They burned under the ceiling lights.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.750
173 just waited.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.540
This wasn’t a contest she could win.

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:58.750
In a final moment of terror, the researcher
was forced to finally close her eyes and she

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:00.420
waited for the crunch.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:01.540
But it never came.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:05.390
Instead, she heard familiar high pitched squeaking
noises.

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:13.310
She opened her eyes, crying tears of relief,
as she saw SCP-131-A sitting behind 173, watching

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:16.610
it with its constant, unblinking gaze.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:21.000
The Killer Sculpture was paralyzed by a cheerful
little Safe-Class anomaly.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:26.080
Across the facility, a similar situation had
unfolded with SCP-689.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:32.060
The statue of death had claimed many lives,
but SCP-131-B had swooped in and frozen the

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:35.320
statue in place with its never ending gaze.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:41.200
Soon after, a Mobile Task Force with vision-blocking
visors used advanced echo-location technology

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:46.030
to collect SCP-689 and return it to its containment
cell.

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:50.600
Everyone who’d seen the anomaly was, as
standard protocol dictates, gathered up for

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:51.950
later termination.

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:57.510
Meanwhile, a Mobile Task Force returned the
paralyzed 173 back to its containment cell

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:58.840
with a forklift.

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:04.240
No containment breach is ever a picnic, containment
breaches with multiple dangerous anomalies

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:10.390
are even less so, but the heroic role that
SCP-131 played in bringing things back under

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.690
control was indispensable.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:17.610
After all, it’s not just raw power that
counts when it comes to anomalies.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:23.050
The only anomalous power 131 needed to save
the entire site was its ability to keep looking

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:24.930
when nobody else could.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:29.680
They’re so effective in this role that they’ve
been seriously considered for permanent roles

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:34.660
as “wardens” for SCPs like 173 and 689.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:37.440
And in our opinion, they’re more than qualified.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:45.150
Now check out “SCP - 999 - The Tickle Monster”
and “SCP - 5031 - Yet Another Murder Monster”

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:49.910
for more surprisingly wholesome anomalies
under the care of the SCP Foundation!

